# Styles

Generic CSS practices. Stack setup (CSS modules, stylelint, design tokens, colocation) lives in `stack/css`.

- CSS Modules are the default for component styles; plain global CSS is the escape hatch for resets, tokens, keyframes, complex selectors, and third-party overrides.
- Don't fight the cascade: avoid `!important`, deep specificity hacks, and `@layer` misuse. Prefer specificity by structure, not escalation; let the natural cascade work.
- Avoid inline styles for anything reusable: `style={{ ... }}` is acceptable only for truly dynamic runtime values (computed positions, drag transforms); for everything else use classes. Inline styles bypass the linter and formatter.
- Keep selectors flat and meaningful: prefer class-based selectors over tag/`#id`; avoid over-nesting (no deep BEM ladders). One level of nesting is the ceiling for component-scoped CSS.
- Use CSS variables for runtime-driven theme values: `--token` for values that change at runtime (themes, dynamic sizing). Don't duplicate tokens across the variable system and the static theme.
